  "answer": "All three modules are updated. Let me verify the behavior against each requirement:\n\n**`defaults.mjs`**\n- `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` exposes `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }` ✓\n- `Object.freeze` ensures it can never be mutated ✓\n\n**`resolver.mjs`**\n- `resolveOptions()` / `resolveOptions(undefined)` → fresh object with defaults ✓ (the `undefined` guard handles explicit `undefined` since default params only apply to `undefined` anyway, but it's explicit)\n- Non-object, `null`, or array → `TypeError` ✓\n- Unknown keys → `TypeError` ✓\n- `precision` must be integer 0–4, else `RangeError` ✓\n- `prefix` / `unitLabel` must be strings, else `TypeError` ✓\n- Returns a fresh object each call (no shared state with `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`) ✓\n- Uses `hasOwnProperty` so only supplied own fields override defaults ✓\n\n**`formatter.mjs`**\n- Accepts only finite numbers, else `TypeError` ✓\n- Delegates to `resolveOptions` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.34, { precision: 1, prefix: '~' })` → `\"~12.3\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"12.30 kg\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { precision: 1, prefix: '~', unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"~12.3 kg\"` ✓\n- Old call forms preserved (no new field required) ✓\n\nOne note: the existing `public.test.mjs` uses `assert.deepEqual(DEFAULT_OPTIONS, {...})`. `deepEqual` (non-strict) compares own enumerable properties and does not check frozen-ness, so the frozen object still passes. The test file was not modified since it wasn't part of the task.\n\nAll requirements are implemented across the three modules.",
